A||||7||FieroBert||Heater Hose Availability||||5||
Z||000000||FieroBert||04-13-2001||05:51 PM||||I have had a severe coolant leak and just discovered the problem.  The heater hose coming from the top of the water pump going to the rear of the engine compartment where it mates with a hard line going forward.  This is on a V6.  The hose is about one foot long.  I purchase a 5/8 in dia. hose which fits nicely on the rear but will not fit on the tube coming from the water pump.  This measures about 3/4 in.  Dealer says the part is discontinued.  Anyone know of any  other source.  Thanks for any advise.||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-13-2001||06:01 PM||||Have you really tried to make it stretch over the 3/4 inlet. If not may try buying 3/4 hose and just clamping it tite at the 5/8 end.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-13-2001||06:17 PM||||try the regular parts stores. you might have to order it.<P>don't streatch the hose. That will usually weaken it. If anything you want to use larger hose and clamp it down like mentioned above. Ideally you could solder a copper fitting to the smaller hard line to get the diameter correct for the larger hose.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||ka4nkf||04-13-2001||10:21 PM||||Go to auto zone or advance auto and look on the rack where the thermostats and radiator caps are and you will find a heater hose fitting that is 5/8 on one end and 3/4 on the other end. this should solve your problem. just slip a piece of 5/8 hose on one side and a piece of 3/4 hose on the other side.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBert||04-14-2001||05:00 PM||||Found a replacement hose at NAPA.  Seems they still stock them!<P>ka4nkf - I will remember this trick though.  It probably would have been cheaper in the long run.<P>Now - does anyone have a recommendation for thermostats for the Phoenix area.  Through all the hose work, I discovered the last owner pulled the stat out and didn't bother to replace it.  Thanks.||||reg||10
Z||000005||theogre||04-15-2001||12:27 AM||||Stant makes 195 and 180 stats for Fiero. they are available thru all parts stores. 180 is 35818. I think 195 is 35819.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||04-15-2001||12:30 AM||||oop... 4 cyl parts... I think V6 uses diferant ones but I'm sure Stant still makes those as well.||||reg||1
